      "text": "The Coast Guard has awarded an historic $400 million contract to modernize Training Center Cape May, which is home to the service’s boot camp for new recruits. \n\nThis project is the largest shore construction award in Coast Guard history and allows for the construction of new barracks buildings, a new multi-purpose training facility and other improvements at TRACEN Cape May. \n\nWith recruit numbers projected to surpass 8,000 annually by 2030, this strategically phased transformation will ensure our campus is fully prepared to meet future demands.\n\nAt Cape May, and across the Coast Guard, our unmatched return on America’s investment continues.\n\nMore details: https://t.co/vzF7SDDmCv",
      "text_resolved": "The Coast Guard has awarded an historic $400 million contract to modernize Training Center Cape May, which is home to the service’s boot camp for new recruits. \n\nThis project is the largest shore construction award in Coast Guard history and allows for the construction of new barracks buildings, a new multi-purpose training facility and other improvements at TRACEN Cape May. \n\nWith recruit numbers projected to surpass 8,000 annually by 2030, this strategically phased transformation will ensure our campus is fully prepared to meet future demands.\n\nAt Cape May, and across the Coast Guard, our unmatched return on America’s investment continues.\n\nMore details: https://tinyurl.com/uyxdy8ua",
